			},
			"date": "2025-08-04T14:28:59.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> the transform method does use attributes, yeah. If you’re wanting programmatic access to each image transformation, the transform method is likely not for you. (use the shortcode method instead?) I’d subscribe to something like <a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/eleventy-img/issues/248\"><span>https://</span><span>github.com/11ty/eleventy-img/i</span><span>ssues/248</span></a> for future work there</p>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/11ty/eleventy-img/issues/248\">Does eleventy-img have a callback for each transformation? · Issue #248 · 11ty/eleventy-img</a>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
